[Javaagent] For multi-class `hasClassesNamed(...)` checks the convention is to place a version comment directly above each class name string, not next to the outer `.and(`. If `com.alipay.sofa.rpc.transport.ClientHandler` was added in 5.4.0 and uniquely identifies the library (its package is already SOFARPC-specific), the `com.alipay.sofa.rpc.filter.Filter` check looks redundant and the compact single-class form would be preferable:

```suggestion
    // added in 5.4.0
    return hasClassesNamed("com.alipay.sofa.rpc.transport.ClientHandler");
```

If `Filter` really is needed as a second landmark, keep both but put a version comment above each class string per the multi-class convention.

