threads.body:
[Javaagent] The repo's `*Singletons` convention for lower-camel collaborator fields (e.g. `Filter` instances, `Instrumenter`s, helpers) is `private static final` + same-name accessor method, with callers static-importing the accessor:

```java
private static final Filter clientFilter;
private static final Filter serverFilter;

public static Filter clientFilter() { return clientFilter; }
public static Filter serverFilter() { return serverFilter; }
```

The existing `apache-dubbo-2.7` `DubboSingletons` uses the uppercase `public static final` form too, so this is a pre-existing pattern in a sibling module — flagging only so you can opt into the newer convention here if desired; otherwise parity with dubbo is fine.

