threads.body:
[Testing] `timeout()` sleeps 2000 ms, and if `Thread.sleep` is interrupted it still returns `"timeout"` normally. The corresponding test configures the consumer with a 1000 ms timeout and expects `SofaTimeOutException` on the client, but the server impl still completes a second later and emits another SERVER span, which can flake timing-sensitive assertions. Consider blocking much longer (or indefinitely) and failing on interrupt so the server side doesn't produce a late "success" response after a client timeout:

```suggestion
  @Override
  public String timeout() {
    try {
      Thread.sleep(10_000);
    } catch (InterruptedException e) {
      Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
      throw new IllegalStateException(e);
    }
    return "timeout";
  }
```

